    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0159" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/218: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)<anchor n="39" xml:id="d163-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-25T13:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. Your 237, July 17. Department agrees with your view that it would be
                    preferable to handle food matters through a subcommittee of CSC rather than an
                    independent body. Soviet representatives might be invited to sit on subcommittee
                    in advisory capacity if it should be found necessary.</p>
                <p>With respect to British Minister’s suggestion that Iranian Ministry of Food be
                    established, Department would authorize you to support this proposal, provided
                        <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) you think idea would be acceptable to
                    Iranians and <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) you are convinced such a Ministry
                    would increase efficiency in food supply matters within a reasonable time.
                    However, in view of inevitable delays in organization and resulting confusion,
                    we are inclined to think it would be well to postpone any such undertaking at
                    least pending the arrival of an American food and supply adviser.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="39" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom as telegram No. 3460, July 25,
                    noon.</p>
            </note>
